{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development fails to demonstrate how additional parking could be accommodated in the immediate area without contributing to parking stress. The proposal would also discourage sustainable travel options, and would exceed the maximum residential parking standards for an area located within PTAL 5. The proposal would therefore be contrary to policy which seek to ensure that developments promote sustainable travel:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policies T1 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "The proposed development, by reason of its design, bulk, mass, scale and siting, would appear out-keeping with the prevailing character of the host dwelling, the terrace row, and the distinctiveness and historic character of the Becontree Estate. The proposal would result in a detrimental loss of symmetry of the existing terrace row and a&nbsp;loss of the open aspect and visual amenity of this plot. It would thereby cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the area, including&nbsp;moderate&nbsp;harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
